# Mail spool backlog on the batch-prod host.
#
# The spool is a file queue drained by supervisor's mail-spooler daemon(s). A
# backlog means mail is being generated faster than it is delivered, and it is
# otherwise SILENT: the generating crons succeed, postfix on the smarthost is
# healthy, and the only symptom is mail arriving hours late. On 2026-08-18 it
# reached 67k / 8 hours and the first anyone knew was a person noticing their
# hourly donation summary had not arrived.
#
# 20000 for 15 cycles (= 30 min at 120s/cycle). A digest run legitimately
# queues tens of thousands and drains them, so the threshold alone would be
# noise; it is the SUSTAINED part that means "not draining". At the observed
# drain rate a 20k queue clears in ~20 min, so still being over it after 30
# means delivery is genuinely not keeping up.
check program mail-spool-backlog with path "/etc/monit/scripts/mail-spool-backlog.sh 20000"
   group mail
   if status != 0 for 15 cycles then alert
